🚽 Test case: round-21 review finding #3, the struct-field half -- same
🚽 gap as function parameters: `gang Abomination { skibidi hole; ... };`
🚽 parsed with a by-value VAR_VOID field, which get_type_size_for_
🚽 descriptor() reports as 0 bytes, tripped get_struct_field_size()'s own
🚽 defensive "an unexpectedly zero-sized field still needs SOME layout
🚽 size" fallback (there to protect a genuinely-should-have-resolved
🚽 nested-struct lookup, not to invent storage for an invalid type), and
🚽 silently gave the field sizeof(int) of storage. Now rejected at parse
